## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design secure, scalable multi-tenant inference with cross-account PrivateLink, model registry usage, and drift-aware rollouts under cost constraints.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines
- PrivateLink across AWS accounts
- Multi-tenant isolation strategies (shared vs. per-tenant containers)
- Drift detection with SageMaker Clarify
- Canary rollout and rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function routeTenant(input, modelRegistry) {
  const tenant = input.tenantId;
  if (!allowedTenants.has(tenant)) {
    throw new Error('Unauthorized tenant');
  }
  const modelVersion = modelRegistry.getModelVersion(tenant, 'latest');
  return invokeSageMaker(modelVersion.endpoint, input);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical deployment choices that balance latency, cost, and data locality for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Endpoint configuration and quantization
- Auto-scaling by latency target
- Canary rollouts for low-risk deployment
- Data residency and basic validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// setup autoscaling (simplified)
import { ApplicationAutoScalingClient, RegisterScalableTargetCommand, PutScalingPolicyCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-application-auto-scaling';
const c = new ApplicationAutoScalingClient({region: 'us-east-1'});
async function cfg(){
  await c.send(new RegisterScalableTarget({
    ServiceNamespace: 'sagemaker',
    ResourceId: 'endpoint/my-image-endpoint/variant/AllTraffic',
    ScalableDimension: 'sagemaker:variant:DesiredInstanceCount',
    MinCapacity: 1,
    MaxCapacity: 20
  }));
  await c.send(new PutScalingPolicy({
    PolicyName: 'LatencyTarget',
    PolicyType: 'TargetTrackingScaling',
    ServiceNamespace: 'sagemaker',
    ResourceId: 'endpoint/my-image-endpoint/variant/AllTraffic',
    ScalableDimension: 'sagemaker:variant:DesiredInstanceCount',
    TargetTrackingScalingPolicyConfiguration: {
      TargetValue: 200
    }
  }));
}
```

